# Ocean Simulation Action Plan

Target reference:
`game/shaders/dual_jonswap_ocean_fft.comp.slang`

Current prototype:
- `game/shaders/source/ocean/generate_jonswap.comp.slang`
- `game/shaders/source/ocean/ocean.vert.slang`
- `game/shaders/source/ocean/ocean.frag.slang`
- `game/src/ocean.odin`

The current convention is now correct and should be treated as locked:
- world is Z-up
- ocean mesh lies in XY
- horizontal displacement = `displacement.x`, `displacement.y`
- vertical displacement = `displacement.z`
- vertex shader adds `spec.xyz` directly (`ocean.vert.slang:61-62`)
- Jacobian uses the `x/y` horizontal pair (`generate_jonswap.comp.slang:215-218`)

Do not change this convention during the FFT port. Instead, adapt the reference
(which uses X/Z horizontal and Y up) to this convention.

