## Phase 0 - Stabilize the current prototype before starting the FFT

Do this first. The FFT will be much harder to debug if the current prototype
still has ambiguous spectrum scaling or a broken fold correction.

✅✅✅ 0.1 Lock and document the axis convention✅✅✅

✅ - Keep `x/y` horizontal and `z` up.
✅ -  Rename local coordinates in `main` if needed so the second texture axis is
  clearly `y`, not `z` (`generate_jonswap.comp.slang:93-94`).
✅ - Add a short comment in each ocean file stating the convention:
  `x = right, y = forward, z = up`.
✅ - Check `inc_ocean.slang`, `ocean.vert.slang`, `ocean.frag.slang`, and
  `generate_jonswap.comp.slang` all use the same `OceanData` layout.

 ✅✅✅ 0.2 Replace the per-texel Jacobian correction with global choppiness ✅✅✅

Current code multiplies the horizontal displacement by a per-texel
`saturate(J / 0.1)` mask (`generate_jonswap.comp.slang:245-255`). This creates
new folds because the scale field itself has a large spatial gradient.

Do this:
✅ - Remove the `dynamic_scale` multiply from `displacement.x/y`.
- Always write the raw displacement plus `J` into the output texture.
✅ - Add a global `lambda`/choppiness parameter. Apply it to the horizontal
  displacement only:
  ✅ - `displacement.x *= lambda`
  ✅ - `displacement.y *= lambda`
  ✅ - leave `displacement.z` as height.
✅ - Start with `lambda = 0.5`, tune down until folds are rare.
✅ - Keep `J` in `.w` for foam and debugging.
✅ - Only after the FFT is stable should you consider a more advanced fold-aware
  geometry correction.

This matches the reference strategy: `_Lambda` scales horizontal displacement
while `J` is used for foam (`dual_jonswap_ocean_fft.comp.slang:318-335`).

✅✅✅ 0.3 Make the current spectrum meaningful ✅✅✅

The current `jonswap_energy` is a simplified prototype. `windSpeed`, `fetch`,
`shortWavesFade`, `alignment`, and `compute_peaking` are currently unused or
ignored. For the FFT version this will cause the spectrum to be mis-scaled.

Do this before porting:
- Decide whether the simulation is parameterized by frequency or wavenumber. Note: This will likely change with the migration to fft, don't worry about this for now.
- Keep the deep-water mapping `k = omega^2 / g` for the current generator.
- Add the missing JONSWAP constants:
  ✅ - alpha from wind/fetch
  ✅ - peak frequency
  ✅ - gamma / storm maturity
  ✅ - sigma split at the peak
  ✅ - short-wave fade
  ✅ - directional spread
- Use `oceanography.slang` as the local reference for JONSWAP,
  Pierson-Moskowitz, TMA, and directional spread.
- Cross-check against `dual_jonswap_ocean_fft.comp.slang:58-131`.
- Remove dead code (`compute_peaking`, `rollover_fix_delta`, unused derivative
  variables) or wire it in deliberately.

Important for the FFT port: the normalization is different between frequency
bands and wavenumber cells:
- frequency-band amplitude: `sqrt(2 * E * delta_f)`
- FFT initialization: `sqrt(2 * S(omega) * abs(domega/dk) / k * delta_k^2)`
  (`dual_jonswap_ocean_fft.comp.slang:158-166`)

✅✅✅ 0.4 Add debug views and controls ✅✅✅

Add a debug mode before FFT work:
✅ - visualize displacement X, Y, Z
✅ - visualize Jacobian `J`
✅ - visualize `lambda` and fold masks
✅ - log/display min/max/NaN statistics for displacement and `J`

Add UI controls for:
✅ - `lambda` / choppiness
✅ - wave scale
✅ - wind speed
✅ - fetch
✅ - peak frequency
✅ - storm maturity / gamma
✅ - layer count (prototype only)
✅ - time scale and pause

### 0.5 Validate the prototype

- Confirm waves are vertical, not sideways.
- Confirm phase speed matches `omega / k`.
- Confirm wavelength matches `2*pi / k`.
- Confirm the texture wraps without seams.
- Confirm no NaNs and no Vulkan validation errors.
- Confirm the per-texel spikes are gone after switching to global `lambda`.

Exit criteria for Phase 0:
- The current ocean is stable, correctly oriented, and fold-free with tuned
  `lambda`.
- `J` is available for debugging/foam.
- No NaN or validation errors.
- The spectrum parameters are understood well enough to port.

