## Phase 2 - Make the spectrum high quality

### 2.1 Proper JONSWAP parameterization

- use `alpha` from wind/fetch instead of a hand-tuned scale
- use the correct peak frequency relation
- use `gamma` / storm maturity correctly
- use the asymmetric sigma split
- add TMA correction for finite depth
- add short-wave fade
- add directional spreading (Donelan-Banner / Cosine2s / Hasselmann)
- add optional swell

References:
- `dual_jonswap_ocean_fft.comp.slang:58-131`
- `game/shaders/source/ocean/oceanography.slang`

### 2.2 Wavenumber-domain normalization

- verify `delta_k`, `domega/dk`, and the `sqrt(...)` normalization
- verify the integrated variance matches the requested significant wave height
- verify the peak wavelength matches the peak period
- verify that changing `scale` or `alpha` does not silently change the peak shape

### 2.3 Multiple cascades

Use separate length scales and spectra:
- large cascade: long swell
- medium cascade: wind sea
- small cascade: detail
- optional second spectrum per cascade for swell/wind-sea mixture

Reference:
- `_LengthScale0.._LengthScale3` (`18-19`)
- per-cascade spectrum pairs (`138-166`)

### 2.4 Cascade blending and tiling

- sample displacement/slope maps from all cascades
- blend by distance/LOD
- keep tiling seamless
- fade cascades out before their Nyquist limit
- avoid double-counting energy between cascades

Exit criteria for Phase 2:
- the ocean looks correct at all distances
- no visible cascade seams or popping
- wave height/period respond physically to wind/fetch/peak settings
- energy is conserved across cascades

