### 5.1 Performance

- profile each compute pass
- choose FFT size vs cascade count
- use FP16 where possible
- pack fields to reduce bandwidth
- avoid redundant spectrum updates when parameters are unchanged
- avoid CPU/GPU stalls
- consider async compute for the FFT chain
- keep the number of cascades and texture samples reasonable

### 5.2 Robustness

- validate every image layout/barrier
- check for NaN/Inf in displacement and `J`
- handle window resize
- handle shader hot reload
- handle parameter changes without reallocating every frame
- add a fallback/debug path if the FFT fails

### 5.3 Tests

- CPU FFT reference test
- spectrum integration test
- peak frequency/wavelength test
- Jacobian sign test on a known wave
- cascade energy test
- visual regression screenshots
- Vulkan validation in debug builds

Exit criteria for Phase 5:
- stable frame time
- no validation errors
- deterministic results across runs
- no memory growth

